A||||14||Spektrum-87GT||are the 2.8 fieros loud stock?||||1||
Z||000000||Spektrum-87GT||11-23-2001||07:41 PM||||mines kinda loud... doesnt annoy anyone, its just.. well.. loud! i've only heard two other gts on the road, one sounded like mine and the other i didnt hear at all. is there a common problem with the muffler on the 2.8 or are they all just have a nice exhaust note?||||reg||1
Z||000001||88CoupeV6||11-23-2001||08:13 PM||||I think there all that way. Every one I've been around anyway.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  I love it<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88coupeV6.jpg">       <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>    <A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com/nefa.htm" TARGET=_blank>Join New England Fiero Association</A>||||reg||10
Z||000002||fierochild||11-23-2001||08:26 PM||||They're loud if the cat isn't clogged.  Bought an 86 GT back in February. Sounded good but muffled. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I thought that's the way in is suppose to sound till the cat exploded.<BR>Split half into, and got REAL loud. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_drunk.gif"> Took the cat off and put in a temp straight pipe.  I love the sound though a bit loud. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Unfortunately,  I will have to put the cat back on for emissions <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P><BR>86 Lambo Green GT<BR>Fierochild||||reg||1
Z||000003||Smoooooth GT||11-23-2001||09:41 PM||||I don't have a cat either.. just the ole' straight pipe with the series 80 Flowmaster!!! AND  IT SOUND'S TOUGH!!!!<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Smooooth_Yellow_sig_3.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/texas_1.gif">          <BR>Shaved door handles, sidetrim, exhaust outlet's, etc.... smooooth!!!||||reg||1
Z||000004||CoolBlue87GT||11-23-2001||11:03 PM||||Well, I guess I can answer this one.<P>With my 1700 miles & all being 100% stock.<P>I think the V6 is somewhat loud, but within an acceptable range.<P>It seems like when it's cold -(warming up, just started) that it's a little louder when first reving it up.<P>I especialy like the 'bark' while downshifting to slow down for a light.<P>I had an 85 SE w/V6 & it sounded the same way.<P>For the 90K + miles I put on the 85, it sounded the same as day one when I traded it in.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/CoolBluesig.gif"> ||||reg||6
Z||000005||FieroGTChile87||11-24-2001||12:26 AM||||Yeah, my GT's pretty loud. It sounds fairly deep and throaty and the note seems to travel. What I like about the Fiero's exhaust is that it's respondent. My friend who has a 98 Mustang GT says that he loves my car's exhaust. It's considerably louder than his Mustang at low speeds but of course his sounds more powerful when he gets on it.<P>------------------<BR>Maroon 87 GT<BR>Gold 87 SE V6 (Disabled)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroGTChile_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||artherd||11-24-2001||03:22 AM||||The Stock catalysts were very restrictive, and had quite a muffeling effect of their own.  Thus, the muffler GM chose for our cars is a rather 'extreme' low-restriction design (read; it's loud  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>When we replace our catalysts with modern, low-restriction designs, we loose the muffeling (and 10-odd horsepower loss) of the old cats.<P>Makes the car pretty loud for an essentially stock production road vehicle!  Cool  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000007||Indy-2M4||11-24-2001||09:10 AM||||My new 87 GT is kinda loud and my hubby's 86 SE is the same. Very exotic sounding, I think!||||reg||1
Z||000008||FieroPerformance||11-24-2001||10:18 AM||||In the rare occation that I am following my car in another car, it sounds really loud. I love it. It came stock with something all the Honda owners are trying to imitate, and then they call it old. It sounds better than any Honda that I've ever heard.<P>-Charlie<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsigfperformance.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||WKDFIRO||11-24-2001||12:10 PM||||What some other people thought about the stock exhaust note a few years ago... <P>(Im still trying to backtrack the dates)<P>"The new exhaust note is a beautiful rasp, and the V-6 is smooth and sweet all the way to the 6000 rpm redline."<BR>-Car and Driver, Nov 1984<P>"The 2.8 liter, fuel injected six is a strong running, free-breathing powerplant with a sound track fit for a Maserati."<BR>	-Car and Driver<P>"The note is absolutely perfect."<BR>	-Automobile<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000010||avengador1||11-24-2001||12:36 PM||||It does sound sweet to the ears. I have the Ocelot exhaust system and a free flow cat and I don't consider it loud, but my wife says the whole house rumbles when I rev it up in the garage. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||firstfiero||11-24-2001||01:19 PM||||   My favorite thing about my girl! The first time I got it inspected they swore something was wrong. lol<P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||SLYGUY||11-24-2001||01:42 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by artherd:<BR><B><BR> pretty loud for an essentially stock production road vehicle!  Cool   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I agree. My car is very quiet until you get into it. Very nice deep bass from the exhaust. I especially like the bass when you lug it just a little from a stop in first gear.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000013||SKIDMARK||11-24-2001||02:44 PM||||My 2.8 was pretty loud! I think the holes in the cat contributed to the noise. It was really noticable with the sunroof open. To tell the truth, it sounded about the same with or without the exhaust hooked up, at least from inside the car. I had several people tell me it sounded "throaty". You could definitely pick it out by the sound in a group of Fieros.<BR>My buddies 85 SE V-6 is pretty quiet in comparison. Doesn't have that rumble to it.<P>------------------<BR>White '85 4cyl coupe<BR>Black '86 v-6 SE<BR>'81 CB900F Super Sport<p>[This message has been edited by SKIDMARK (edited 11-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||jubjub2m6||11-25-2001||12:49 AM||||I wouldnt say that the stock exhaust is loud it sounds pretty meaty really...but i would suggest putting either like a flowmaster or a borla exhaust on it..you wanna hear meaty i put the flowmaster and 3" twin tips on each size it sure sounds really meaty people think twice about trying to race me now since my car sounds so mean...gotta love that glub blub sound||||reg||1
